  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Request flow & access",
      "items": [
        "Admin submits locations, time windows, vehicles, and traffic settings; FastAPI invokes the selected existing algorithm and returns routes.",
        "Admin dispatches the plan; drivers retrieve it and report completed stops. Admin / Driver roles are client-side; the API routes shown have no authentication middleware."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Data & state",
      "items": [
        "RC101, RC201, and C101 Solomon CSVs feed benchmark runs; benchmark endpoints read the existing summary CSV and statistics JSON.",
        "Jobs, active dispatch, and driver progress live in API-process dictionaries. No Redis / PostgreSQL integration is configured; a process restart clears this state."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Mapping & traffic",
      "items": [
        "The browser loads OpenStreetMap tiles directly; FastAPI proxies road geometry and turn steps to OSRM. QMAPS_OSRM_BASE_URL replaces the public default.",
        "Preset scenarios and admin-entered corridor delays modify modeled travel; the runtime does not read a live traffic feed."
      ]
    }
  ]
